    {
      "id": "1553915815256920204",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-27T23:46:40.717+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "> Yes I have, but they seem to have too much friction for precision applications or induce play if they are manufactured with a loose fit.\nThis one in particular regarding these makes me wonder if the DIY porous graphite block spherical air bearings AppliedScience demonstrated a few years back would scale/be approriate, as AFAIK those can be set up to have no stiction and the air in the gap acts first order as a pretty linear spring which would imply decently behaved kinematic modeling and should at least for sufficiently limited-required-stiffness applications provide acceptable \"lack of wiggle/play\".....",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-09_media/f885abc0dddd0a33e4d4991b3c99091d-7ACD2.png"
      },
      "attachments": [
        {
