      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Also Z conveninetly is much tamer in distance requirements and can likley use a lot of force-control motion for at least corase movement/until-touch to sort of \"home\" itself to a position right where it's touching and then hold while e.g. resin hardens or e.g. move a defined small distance further to compress ACF (anisotropic conductive film) tape or squash down sintering paste or such....",
